PURPOSE
-------
Migrate authentication from Keycloak to Supabase Auth, and migrate the
application database from MySQL to PostgreSQL (Supabase PostgreSQL).

Current state:
- Keycloak 23.0.7 handles OAuth2/JWT for the API gateway and user management
- MySQL 8.4.0 is used by all four data services
- Flyway MySQL migrations manage the core-banking-service schema

Target state:
- Supabase Auth provides JWT tokens (RS256) and user management admin API
- PostgreSQL (Supabase-hosted or self-hosted) replaces MySQL for all services
- Flyway PostgreSQL migrations manage the core-banking-service schema
- Frontend uses Supabase email/password credentials via NextAuth instead of Keycloak SSO redirect

QUESTIONS & ANSWERS
-------------------
No blocking questions — scope is clear from codebase analysis and user request.

DECISIONS MADE
--------------
1. Replace keycloak-admin-client with direct HTTP calls to Supabase Admin Auth API
   using Spring's RestClient (available in Spring Boot 3.2) — no new dependency needed.

2. Replace MySQL connector with PostgreSQL driver (org.postgresql:postgresql) in all
   four data services. Spring Boot BOM manages the version.

3. Remove flyway-mysql from core-banking-service; flyway-core supports PostgreSQL natively.
   Rewrite existing Flyway SQL migrations to PostgreSQL syntax (BIGSERIAL, no backtick
   quoting, standard FK constraints).

4. Keep NextAuth in the frontend but replace KeycloakProvider with a Credentials
   provider that calls supabase.auth.signInWithPassword(). This keeps all
   useSession() usages intact without component rewrites.

5. Add @supabase/supabase-js to the frontend — used in auth.ts credentials authorize().

6. Docker-compose: remove keycloak_web, keycloakdb, mysql_core_db; add a local
   PostgreSQL 15 container (postgres_app_db) for local development. Services receive
   datasource and Supabase config via environment variables which override Config Server.

7. API gateway JWT validation is config-only: the property
   spring.security.oauth2.resourceserver.jwt.jwk-set-uri is overridden via env var
   SPRING_SECURITY_OAUTH2_RESOURCESERVER_JWT_JWK-SET-URI pointing to
   {SUPABASE_URL}/auth/v1/.well-known/jwks.json. No code change in SecurityConfiguration.

8. User account creation flow: create Supabase user with email_confirm: false (pending).
   On APPROVED status update, call Supabase admin API to set email_confirm: true
   (mirrors Keycloak enabled: false → enabled: true flow).

ALTERNATIVES CONSIDERED
-----------------------
- Self-hosted Supabase (docker): More portable but requires 20+ containers; out of scope
  for a concept project migration. Using cloud Supabase + local postgres for dev.
- Replace NextAuth entirely with @supabase/auth-helpers-nextjs: Requires rewriting all
  page components that use useSession() — too disruptive for this migration.
- Use Spring WebClient instead of RestClient: Both are reactive, but RestClient is the
  recommended synchronous HTTP client in Spring Boot 3.2+; WebClient would require
  extra unwrapping in a blocking context.
- Use Feign client for Supabase Admin API: Possible but adds a new FeignClient interface
  just for external auth calls; RestClient is simpler and already available.

SCOPE OF CHANGES
----------------
Affected services: internet-banking-user-service, core-banking-service,
                   internet-banking-fund-transfer-service,
                   internet-banking-utility-payment-service,
                   internet-banking-api-gateway (config only),
                   internet-banking-frontend
Affected layers  : service, config, build (dependencies), DB migrations,
                   docker-compose, frontend auth/login
New endpoints    : none
Schema changes   : Flyway migrations rewritten for PostgreSQL syntax (BIGSERIAL,
                   standard constraints); no table/column renames
New dependencies : @supabase/supabase-js (frontend npm); org.postgresql:postgresql
                   (Java — replaces mysql-connector-j)
Removed deps     : org.keycloak:keycloak-admin-client:24.0.4,
                   com.mysql:mysql-connector-j:8.4.0 (all 4 services),
                   org.flywaydb:flyway-mysql:10.12.0 (core-banking only),
                   next-auth KeycloakProvider import (frontend)

External config note: The Spring Cloud Config Server external repository
(https://github.com/JavatoDev-com/internet-banking-microservices-configurations.git)
also needs its datasource URLs and JWK URI updated. Docker-compose env var overrides
remove this dependency for local/docker runs.

RISKS & NOTES
-------------
- Supabase Admin API filter=email performs text search, not exact match; the service
  layer does exact-match comparison after fetching results.
- Flyway checksums: since we are migrating to a fresh PostgreSQL database, Flyway
  history is empty and rewritten migration files run cleanly.
- Token refresh: NextAuth credentials provider does not auto-refresh Supabase tokens.
  For the concept project this is acceptable; production would use Supabase auth helpers
  with proper PKCE + refresh handling.
- PostgreSQL sequence reset: temp-data migration inserts with explicit IDs; sequence
  is reset after the inserts so subsequent auto-increments work correctly.
- Config Server: Services in docker-compose override config server values via
  environment variables. Dev profile (bootstrap-dev.yml) still points to Config Server;
  update those properties in the external repo for non-docker dev.

